-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Quazatron
  Publisher   Hewson, 1986
  Version     1.1

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Quazatron (1986)(Hewson Consultants)[aka Ziggurat].z80
  MD5         ac51eb58af87fdac9c0c7077db98c90a

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Colour, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    The monochrome decks in colour: floors, walls, ramps, arrow
              panels, objects and pads each in their own tone, taken from the
              deck's own colour; every droid painted by its parts as a
              hardware sprite, the player's droid included. The panel below
              the play area is unchanged. A painted set, colourist not named.

  Pace        original

  Changes     1.1: Centred view toggle: the camera follows the player at 50
              frames a second through a velocity filter (steady speed while
              walking, no overshoot when stopping), the player fixed on the
              screen, droids locked to the deck, the game's view stepping
              ahead of the camera; fewer missed interrupts in the pace
              limiter's waits. 1.0: colour scenery on Layer 2 and droids as
              painted sprites over a monochrome base; Smooth scrolling; the
              original's pace kept by a pace limiter

  Note        Kempston: choose 4 on CONTROL SELECTION, ENTER, then fire.
              Colour is the menu's Enhanced colours line: on, the colour game;
              off, the game's own monochrome picture. Smooth scrolling (off by
              default) makes scroll bursts quicker and glides the view.
              Centred view (off by default; turns Smooth scrolling on with it)
              keeps your droid in the middle of the screen with the deck
              gliding underneath, instead of the game's pushes at the screen
              edges: a change to the game, as the view decides which droids
              move. The camera follows your droid at a steady speed, about
              0.12 s behind it. Both have no visible effect in monochrome
              except that Centred view scrolls in single steps there. Pace:
              the default modes keep the original's, within 1%; Centred view
              runs about 2% slower in quiet scenes and 5 to 7% in busy or
              scrolling ones (a fix is planned). Measured in JNext only;
              hardware untested. P pauses; fire resumes.

