-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      1.0 played by the owner in JNext 2026-11-06: approved; 1.1
              played by the owner in JNext 2026-11-06 (Centred view): approved

  Replay      Centred view off: IDENTICAL on v1.0's 6 recordings (c1, b2, b1,
              u2, u3, d1), 25,117 frames, in its 4 states, every hook event
              count equal to v1.0's. Centred view on: IDENTICAL against the
              Centred reference game (the original with the two Centred
              patches and c_pre, the same bytes) on 4 bot recordings of it
              (t5, r6, r7, r8), 16,000 frames, in 4 states; per state 1,096
              one-step scrolls (288 right, 254 left, 288 up, 266 down) at
              2,189 decisions, each matching the rule (per axis: moving that
              way and past the centre), and every settled scroll's background
              equal to a full render (871 checks). Smoothness at every frame:
              the shown player equal to this verifier's own run of the camera
              filter in all 14,744 frames, and the player at (128, 88) on the
              screen in all 12,699 frames with the camera free. Negatives
              detected: the camera filter disabled, ink pass skipped, t_dly R
              delta off by one, sprites with a stale offset (Smooth, and
              Centred), the monochrome gate dropped, the alt ROM fill stopping
              before c_pre, a reference whose step skips its strip render

  Emulator    JNext 1.1.104 headless, v2.09 card: Centred view (colour) walks
              captured frame by frame; nexclash.flicker 300 frames: no figure
              vanished, 7 out-of-step flags against the ULA play area, which
              Layer 2 hides; soak: see notes; both trainers as v1.0

  Coverage    v1.0's coverage, plus the Centred reference: 4 bot recordings
              toward every side of the deck, scrolls in all four directions,
              deck edges, deck changes and deaths (r8: no cheats); not
              reached: lifts, the transfer game, later decks

  Hardware    none

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
